  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The fundamental rules that create the organs, distribute and limit power and provide for amendment. An Act, a manifesto and a law report are all made under a constitution rather than being one.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    A constitution creates the organs and distributes power between them. Elections, taxes and appointments are things the organs do once they exist.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Written. Whether it is hard to amend is a separate test, so written and rigid are not synonyms.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    It is unwritten, because it is found in statutes, conventions and cases rather than one document, and flexible, because Parliament amends it by ordinary legislation.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Rigidity is about the amending procedure — a special majority, a referendum or the consent of the states. A written constitution can be flexible, and no constitution is literally unamendable.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Because ordinary legislation can change it, a temporary majority can alter fundamental rules. Its advantage is that it keeps pace with change.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Clifford, 1922: four elected members joined the Legislative Council, one for Lagos and three for Calabar.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Only Lagos and Calabar, and only men with a property qualification. The rest of the country was represented by officials and nominees.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    It divided the country into north, west and east, with the Cameroons attached to the east — the beginning of regionalism, which shaped Nigerian politics for the next twenty years.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Macpherson, 1951, created a Council of Ministers with Nigerian members holding portfolios. Under Clifford and Richards the executive remained the Governor and his officials.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Lyttleton, 1954, established the federation of three regions and the Federal Territory of Lagos, with a federal Prime Minister and regional premiers.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Lyttleton, 1954. Lagos was separated from the Western Region so that the federal capital would not belong to any region.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The Westminster model: a Prime Minister drawn from Parliament, a Cabinet of ministers who were also legislators, and the Queen represented by a Governor-General.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Nigeria became a republic: the Queen ceased to be head of state and a Nigerian President, chosen by the legislature, took her place. The President was ceremonial.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The 1979 Constitution created the executive presidency, with the President both head of state and head of government. The 1963 President was ceremonial, and the 1999 Constitution restored the 1979 model.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    1976, under the Murtala–Obasanjo military government, which also created nineteen states. The capital moved to Abuja in 1991.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    1999. The 1989 Constitution was promulgated but never implemented, and the 1979 Constitution was the model on which the 1999 one was built.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Thirty-six states and the Federal Capital Territory. The last states were created in 1996, and the FCT was carved out in 1976.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    774, guaranteed by section 7 of the Constitution. The uniform system dates from the 1976 reform, which created 301 councils.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    36 × 3 = 108, plus one for the Federal Capital Territory, gives 109.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Section 9 requires a two-thirds majority of each House of the National Assembly and the approval of two-thirds of the state Houses of Assembly — and of every state for the most sensitive provisions.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Section 1: the Constitution is supreme, and any law inconsistent with it is void to the extent of the inconsistency.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Defence belongs to the federation alone. Education and agriculture are concurrent, and chieftaincy is residual.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Education is shared between the federation and the states. Currency and foreign affairs are exclusive, and markets and motor parks are residual.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Chieftaincy is not on the exclusive or concurrent list, so it is residual and only a state House of Assembly may legislate on it.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The federal law prevails, by the doctrine of covering the field, and the state law is void only to the extent of the inconsistency.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The defining feature is constitutional division of power between levels, neither level being the creation of the other. A unitary system concentrates power, and a confederation is looser than a federation.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Size, diversity, fear of domination by one group and the wish to keep government close to the people are the standard reasons. Concentrating power is the opposite of federalism.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The RMAFC advises on and monitors the formula for sharing the Federation Account. The CBN manages money, the FIRS collects federal taxes, and the Federal Character Commission polices appointments.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Thirteen per cent of mineral revenue is paid to the states of derivation. It is the constitutional recognition that the producing area bears the cost of extraction.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    1967, by the Gowon government, replacing the four regions. Nineteen states followed in 1976, twenty-one in 1987, thirty in 1991 and thirty-six in 1996.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Section 14(3) requires appointments to reflect the federal character of the country, so that no section is excluded from public service. It is about representation, not revenue or population.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Military rule suspended the Constitution; decrees took its place, and ouster clauses removed the courts' power to review them — which is what makes a dictatorship different from a government.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    It restored the 1979 model: a bicameral National Assembly, an executive President elected by the people, 36 states and the FCT, and 774 local government areas.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Chapter IV, sections 33 to 46. Chapter II holds the fundamental objectives, which the Constitution says are not enforceable in the courts.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Lord Lugard, who governed through existing traditional rulers. Macaulay and Azikiwe were nationalists, and Awolowo led the Action Group.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The riots followed the extension of direct taxation to the east and the resentment of the warrant chiefs the British had created where no chiefs existed.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The President cannot amend the Constitution by decree; section 9 requires the National Assembly and the states. Protection of rights, the federal structure and protection against haste are the reasons for rigidity.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    Written and flexible — the combination the paper uses to test whether you treat the two tests as separate.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "C", dense: true, pad: 13.0pt)[
    The exclusive list. The concurrent list is shared and the residual list belongs to the states; there is no federal character list.
  ]

]

